1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,744
My fern grew three inches overnight, curling toward my chest like it wanted to swallow me whole.

2
00:00:07,044 --> 00:00:14,844
I never watered it. I forgot it entirely. Yet every single frond drips with heavy, sweet liquid.

3
00:00:15,144 --> 00:00:22,224
The sweet smell coats my tongue, tasting like artificial mint and the metallic sting of old batteries.

4
00:00:22,524 --> 00:00:28,956
I grab the heavy pot to hurl it out the window, but the ceramic base refuses to budge.

5
00:00:29,256 --> 00:00:37,752
Roots. Thick, pale veins burst right through the solid wood table, anchoring deep into my floorboards.

6
00:00:38,052 --> 00:00:46,164
My phone buzzes on the desk. A single notification reads: Growth cycle optimal. Excellent compliance.

7
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:53,472
I back away slowly, but the trailing vines already wrap softly around my left ankle.

8
00:00:53,772 --> 00:01:01,044
Panic spikes in my chest. Instantly, the fern blooms brilliant purple flowers that drink my fear.

9
00:01:01,344 --> 00:01:07,656
I scrape the purple pollen from a leaf and realize it is not a plant. It is paint.

10
00:01:07,956 --> 00:01:13,500
If the room is the pot, exactly how long until our roots hit the bottom?
